filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-10-16: two of ONLYOFFICE
core's own later fixes to its Word 97-2003 reader, taken back to v9.4.0.129
unchanged - commits 507f0ae06b67c2c6002db653418afd00beba74c0 ("fix bug
#82318", 2026-07-14) and 9848afc4066a1e5c1ff6d640ed11f764303e2f88 ("fix bug
#82612", 2026-07-29) of https://github.com/ONLYOFFICE/core, both after the
v9.4.0.129 tag (AGPL-3.0, Ascensio System SIA).

Measured (2026-10-16): a Word 95 document (nFib 104, saved "complex")
lost its paragraphs - core read its paragraph bin table as Word 97's (32-bit
page numbers) whenever the file says fComplex, so the paragraph pages came
from the wrong offsets and from memory never cleared, and the 3,124
paragraphs of a 96-page document came out as one, with a third of the
text. With ICU's conversion tables (scripts/x2t/icu-data.py) the text itself
decodes; with these fixes the document comes in as the Document Server
reads it: 3,123 paragraphs and the same 515,791 characters. What they
change: the Word 6/95 bin table and paragraph pages whatever fComplex says,
an FKP cleared before it is read and every read of it kept inside its 512
bytes, the character pages checked the same way, and the font table's
names and the string tables read inside their records.

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

